msgid "Code of the register as a whole rather than of one set: its exported procedures and functions are called on the manager, as CalculationRegisters.<Name>.<Function>()."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:404
#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/informationRegister.h:268
msgid "The form the register's list opens with. Empty: the list form is generated from the register's fields."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:414
msgid "Chart of calculation types"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:414
msgid "The chart of calculation types the register is bound to. Every record's CalculationType is a reference into it, and its sections decide the calculation: Displacing - which types cut a record's days, Base - which results its base is made of, Leading - which changes make it stale. Required: the register is not saved without it."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:420
#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/informationRegister.h:271
msgid "Periodicity"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:420
msgid "The grain of the registration period: day, month (the default), quarter or year. A record is registered for the start of its period; a reading as of a moment takes the periods up to the one the moment falls in, and a base without a base period spans the record's registration period at this grain."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:428
#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:251
msgid "Use action period"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:428
msgid "Records carry an action period: the days a record is in force (ActionPeriodStart to ActionPeriodEnd, both inclusive) and the month it is for (ActionPeriod). Needed for displacement: the register's ActualActionPeriod reads what the Displacing types leave of each record. Switching it adds or drops the three columns."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:437
msgid "The schedule the register's calculations read: an information register holding the schedule, the resource that is its value (hours or days) and the dimension that is its date. The schedule data a record reads is this value summed over its days. Available with the action period."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:438
#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegisterMetadataTotals.cpp:1151
msgid "Action period"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:438
msgid "The period the record is FOR: a correction of June registered in July is for June. A record's position - dimensions, type, this period and its days - is what stornos, displacement and recalculation marks are matched by."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:439
msgid "Action period start"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:439
msgid "The first day the record is in force (whole days, the day itself included). With the end it gives the days displacement cuts and the fact reads pieces of."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:440
msgid "Action period end"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:440
msgid "The last day the record is in force, included: a sick leave 12.06-16.06 is five days. A record whose end is before its start has no days and cuts nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:441
#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegisterMetadataTotals.cpp:1154
msgid "Registration period"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:441
msgid "The period the record was entered in, at the start of the register's periodicity. A correction of a closed month is registered in the current one. Readings as of a moment (the Period argument of the virtual tables) and a base without a base period go by it."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:442
msgid "Storno"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:442
msgid "Marks a record that reverses an earlier one: the same position, the figures with the sign turned, registered now. A position's records net out - a storno counts minus one - so a displacer taken back cuts nothing; a storno also answers the recalculation marks of its position."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:447
msgid "Use recalculation"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/calculationRegister.h:447
